  "type": "SoftwareSourceCode",
  "name": "Eoulsan",
  "description": "Eoulsan is a modular and scalable workflow engine dedicated to high-throughput sequencing analyses, designed for bioinformaticians and core facilities. The experimental design is stored in a text file and the workflow steps and parameters in an XML file, which separates the workflow description from the commands to run. It supports bulk RNA-seq, Nanopore long-read RNA-seq, ChIP-seq and single-cell RNA-seq workflows, can reuse Galaxy tool XML wrappers as modules, and runs on workstations, servers and clusters (HTCondor, SLURM, TORQUE) with Docker or Singularity images.",
